lf-contract 0.1
# lf-gcd loops (BEGIN ... WHILE ... REPEAT in lf-euclid): generator v0 has no
# loop invariants, so it reports the word unsupported. Its correctness is
# proved by induction directly on the IR semantics instead (gcd_correct in
# tests/reference/program-ir.lean).
id lf-gcd/0
word lf-gcd
ir tests/program/ir/examples.ir
stack ( a b -- gcd true | false )
inputs a b
statement For integers a, b in the cell range: if either is negative the word returns false; otherwise their greatest common divisor and true.
case a < 0 || b < 0
  out false
case a >= 0 && b >= 0
  out g true
  ensure g >= 0
expect unsupported
